      "id": 1,
      "label": "src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner \u00b7 OwnerController.OwnerController.processFindForm",
      "purpose": "The subsystem groups the **OwnerController** class together with the **OwnerRepository** interface and all of their public methods. Structurally it handles HTTP requests that create, read, update, and search for *Owner* domain objects: it binds request parameters, validates them, builds pagination information, invokes repository queries such as `findByLastNameStartingWith` and `findById`, and returns view names or redirects with model attributes. Because the controller\u2019s methods are tightly coupled to the repository\u2019s query methods and to the `Owner` entity (e.g., accessing `owner.getLastName()`, `BaseEntity.getId()`), they form a cohesive unit that implements the \u201cowner management\u201d use-case of the PetClinic sample application. The unit exists to isolate the web-layer handling of owner-related CRUD and search operations from other concerns (pets, visits, etc.), keeping the routing, validation, pagination, and data-access logic for owners together.",
