      "label": "src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet \u00b7 VetController.VetController.addPaginationModel",
      "purpose": "The subsystem groups the domain model for veterinarians (the **Vet** entity and its collection wrapper **Vets**) together with the data-access layer (**VetRepository**) and the web MVC controller (**VetController**) that presents paginated lists of vets. All of the classes share the same package (`org.springframework.samples.petclinic.vet`) and the controller\u2019s methods call repository queries, manipulate `Page<Vet>` objects, and add pagination attributes to a `Model`, indicating that the unit\u2019s purpose is to retrieve, store, and display veterinarian information in a paginated view. Because the classes are tightly coupled through these calls and share the same concern (handling vet data and its UI representation), they form a cohesive subsystem that isolates the \u201cvet\u201d feature of the PetClinic sample application. The code shown only demonstrates the pagination model preparation; the rest of the subsystem manages the underlying collection of specialties and basic CRUD access for vets.",
