      "id": 3,
      "label": "src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner \u00b7 Pet.Pet",
      "purpose": "The subsystem groups a small hierarchy of domain objects that share a simple \u201cnamed\u201d characteristic. `NamedEntity` provides a `name` field with getter, setter and a `toString` that returns the name, and several concrete entities (`Pet`, `PetType`, `Specialty`) extend it (or at least use the same pattern) to represent core business concepts in the Pet-Clinic sample \u2013 a pet, its type, and a veterinarian\u2019s specialty. These classes expose only basic state-accessors (birth-date, type, a collection of `Visit`s, and methods to add a visit) and therefore are used by many controllers and validators that need to read or modify these attributes. Because they encapsulate the same minimal data model and are tightly coupled through inheritance/composition, they form a cohesive unit that isolates the core \u201cnamed entity\u201d domain model from the rest of the application.",
