      "id": 4,
      "label": "src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model \u00b7 PetClinicRuntimeHints.PetClinicRuntimeHints.registerHints",
      "purpose": "The subsystem groups the core domain model classes (`BaseEntity` and its subclass `Person`) together with the application bootstrap (`PetClinicApplication`) and a Spring Boot runtime-hints provider (`PetClinicRuntimeHints`). Its primary function is to expose these model types for reflection-based serialization and to register static resource patterns (database scripts, message bundles, MySQL config) that the native-image compiler or other runtime-optimisation tools need to know about. By keeping the entity definitions, the main entry point, and the hint registration in one cluster, the build process can treat them as a unit that must be available at startup and during serialization, while the rest of the code (controllers, validators, etc.) simply depends on these classes. The exact business purpose of the entities (e.g., representing a person in the pet-clinic domain) is evident from their names, but the subsystem\u2019s cohesion is driven by the technical requirement to register them for reflection and resource access.",
