      "label": "src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/system \u00b7 WebConfiguration.WebConfiguration.localeChangeInterceptor",
      "purpose": "The five-member subsystem groups together the few Spring Boot configuration and controller classes that provide the *infrastructure* of the Petclinic sample application. `CacheConfiguration` defines a JCache (`javax.cache`) bean (using a `MutableConfiguration` with statistics enabled) that other parts of the app can inject; `WebConfiguration` sets up web-level beans such as a `SessionLocaleResolver` and a `LocaleChangeInterceptor` and registers the interceptor with the MVC interceptor registry, thereby enabling locale-aware request handling. `WelcomeController` supplies a simple endpoint that returns the home page, while `CrashController` deliberately throws a `RuntimeException` (via `triggerException`) to let developers test the application\u2019s error-handling and monitoring pipelines. These classes are clustered together because they all contribute to the \u201csystem\u201d layer \u2013 configuring cross-cutting concerns (caching, locale resolution, MVC interceptors) and exposing minimal diagnostic controllers \u2013 and they do not depend on any domain-specific services, making them a cohesive unit of application-wide infrastructure.",
