      "label": "src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner \u00b7 VisitController.VisitController.processNewVisitForm",
      "purpose": "The six classes in this subsystem are all the methods of **VisitController**, a Spring MVC controller that handles web requests related to creating and editing a veterinary **Visit** for a pet owned by an **Owner**.  \nThe controller\u2019s `loadPetWithVisit` method (shown) fetches an `Owner` from `OwnerRepository`, retrieves the requested `Pet` from that owner, puts both objects into the model, and creates a new `Visit` instance that will be bound to the form. The other methods (`initNewVisitForm`, `processNewVisitForm`, `setAllowedFields`, `minVisitDate`, the constructor) together configure data-binding, enforce validation rules (e.g., disallowing certain fields, ensuring the visit date is not before today), display the form for a new visit, and persist the submitted visit by calling `Owner.addVisit` / `Pet.addVisit`.  \n\nBecause all of these operations revolve around the same request-handling flow\u2014pre-loading the domain objects, preparing the model, validating input, and saving a new `Visit`\u2014they are grouped into a single cohesive unit (the controller) that encapsulates the \u201cadd-visit-to-pet\u201d use case in the PetClinic application.",
